Task 2: Add Variables, Conditionals, and a Multi-Vendor Juniper Template
Subtask 2.1: Create the Juniper Template
Juniper devices use a different configuration syntax (curly-brace hierarchy). Not every interface in real device data has a unit defined (for example, disabled or unused physical interfaces), so the template must guard against a missing unit field.

Create the Juniper template file:
nano templates/juniper/basic_router.j2
Add the following content:
## Configuration for {{ hostname }}
## Generated on {{ generation_date }}
## Device Type: {{ device_type | default('Router') }}

system {
    host-name {{ hostname }};
{% if domain_name %}
    domain-name {{ domain_name }};
{% endif %}
{% if users %}
    login {
{% for user in users %}
        user {{ user.name }} {
            uid {{ user.uid | default(2000 + loop.index) }};
            class {{ user.class | default('operator') }};
            authentication {
                encrypted-password "{{ user.password }}";
            }
        }
{% endfor %}
    }
{% endif %}
    services {
        ssh;
        netconf {
            ssh;
        }
    }
}

{% if interfaces %}
interfaces {
{% for interface in interfaces %}
    {{ interface.name }} {
{% if interface.description %}
        description "{{ interface.description }}";
{% endif %}
{% if interface.unit is defined %}
        unit {{ interface.unit }} {
{% if interface.ip_address %}
            family inet {
                address {{ interface.ip_address }}/{{ interface.prefix_length }};
            }
{% endif %}
        }
{% endif %}
{% if interface.disable is defined and interface.disable %}
        disable;
{% endif %}
    }
{% endfor %}
}
{% endif %}

{% if routing_options %}
routing-options {
{% if routing_options.static_routes %}
{% for route in routing_options.static_routes %}
    static {
        route {{ route.destination }} next-hop {{ route.next_hop }};
    }
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if routing_options.router_id %}
    router-id {{ routing_options.router_id }};
{% endif %}
}
{% endif %}
Note that {% if interface.unit is defined %} wraps the entire unit { ... } block, so interfaces without a unit key (such as a disabled spare interface) simply omit that block instead of rendering broken or empty output.

